menu "PluTO motion profile"

    comment "Starting points: tune them on the bench with the antenna mounted."
    comment "Compile-time constants, unlike the NVS seeds: change, rebuild, flash."

    config PLUTO_MOTION_MAX_SPEED_DEG_S
        int "Top speed of each servo axis (degrees per second)"
        default 60
        range 1 600
        help
            Top speed per axis (HU-36). Below about 20 the pan falls behind
            near the zenith (test_a_high_pass_keeps_up in the rotor tests).

    config PLUTO_MOTION_MAX_ACCEL_DEG_S2
        int "Top acceleration of each servo axis (degrees per second squared)"
        default 120
        range 1 5000
        help
            Top acceleration and deceleration per axis, the braking after a
            HOLD included (HU-36): it spares the gears the jerk of a jump. Too
            low and high passes fall behind as well.

    config PLUTO_MOTION_REST_AFTER_MS
        int "Time still before the servo outputs can be released (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 0 3600000
        help
            Once both axes have been still at the same target this long, both
            servo outputs are released until the next target (HU-35). 0 never
            releases them. If the tilt sags under the antenna without pulses
            (still to be measured), lengthen it or set 0.

endmenu
